I've already got my next purchase picked out, thank goodness they have an online store!"},{"business_id":"y-wuZtF4abISN08EC-VQag","review_id":"PpyAlCvkWxs7OUKQfWlNpA","date":"2015-05-05T20:30:59","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9079599380493164,"text_excerpt":"Once upon a time I chastised my then high-school-age daughter for dropping over $200 on a Coach purse, stating it was ridiculous to spend that much money on something as insignificant as a purse. I sorta made a hypocrite of myself today. I saw an ad for Queork in New Orleans magazine, their stuff was so beautiful I had to check them out. On the pricey side, yes, but it lasts forever and cleans up like new-so if I don't have to buy another purse for years, that's ok, right? So I confessed my hypocrisy to Yelper Daughter and we went into the store today. It's a beautiful store, very clean, elegant, and simple. All the merchandise-bags, shoes, wallets, phone cases, more...is beautiful. I als..."},{"business_id":"y-wuZtF4abISN08EC-VQag","review_id":"IFaMKhLDHYYJtwXAv0J9SQ","date":"2016-09-06T01:48:54","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.8961329460144043,"text_excerpt":"One thing I love about New Orleans: diverse cultural uniqueness at every corner. While walking around looking for a place to eat, we stumbled across this cute little boutique. Their window display caught our attention....cork-like merchandise?! The friendly lady behind the counter greeted us warmly as we looked around. They had purses, hats, bracelets and shoes I thought were so cute! The material is soft to touch. The fedora hats were definitely my favorite. If you're looking for a unique gift to give, this is a great place to stop by."}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
